    "name": "max-gap-an-unfinished-gap-is-reported-rather-than-evaluated",
    "why": "Owner decision I: a gap needs two ends. p-ali's last duty is on the 2nd and the schedule runs to the 31st, so the gap after it has no closing date — measuring it against the edge of the horizon would report twenty-nine days against a limit of five, and would do the same to nearly every person nearly every month, which is a rule a department switches off in its first week. p-noor holds no duty at all and is one open gap over the whole horizon. p-zaid's four-day gap is closed at both ends and is clean, which is what stops the case being green because the type measured nothing. Every one of those five unfinished edges is REPORTED: ignoring them silently is the failure the sibling coverage() exists to prevent.",
